      <ThreadGroup guiclass="ThreadGroupGui" testclass="ThreadGroup" testname="Sustained Tests" enabled="true">
        <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">Main load testing phase with continuous CRUD operations.

CONFIGURATION PARAMETERS (MINIMALIST):
- Threads: 10 concurrent virtual users executing tests simultaneously
- Ramp-Up: 300 seconds - threads start gradually every 30 seconds
- Duration: 600 seconds - TOTAL test runtime from when Thread 1 starts (not additional time after ramp-up!)
- Loop Count: -1 (infinite) - each thread loops continuously until duration expires
- Scheduler: Enabled - uses duration-based execution instead of fixed loop count

CRITICAL CONSTRAINT: Duration MUST be greater than Ramp-Up!
Otherwise later threads won&apos;t start or will have no execution time. With Duration=600s and Ramp-Up=300s,
all threads get meaningful execution time. If Duration was 200s, threads 7-10 would barely run or not start at all.

IMPORTANT TIMING CLARIFICATION:
Duration and ramp-up OVERLAP! The 600 seconds starts when Thread 1 starts, NOT after ramp-up completes.
• Thread 1 gets 600 seconds of execution time (0s → 600s)
• Thread 2 gets 570 seconds of execution time (30s → 600s)
• Thread 10 gets 330 seconds of execution time (270s → 600s)

So threads are actively working during ramp-up - they don&apos;t wait!

EXECUTION FLOW:
• All threads run in parallel once started during the ramp-up period
• Within each thread:
  • Executes all resource groups sequentially (benefits → billto → bin → ... → warehouse)
    NOTE: State resource is handled separately in dedicated Setup/Teardown thread groups
  • Within each resource: POST → GET → PUT → DELETE operations run sequentially
  • After completing all resources (1 complete loop = 96 HTTP requests), immediately starts over
  • Loops continuously until the overall 600-second duration expires

EXAMPLE TIMELINE:
0s: Thread 1 starts executing (benefits POST)
30s: Thread 2 starts, Thread 1 continues working
270s: Thread 10 starts (last thread), Threads 1-9 have been working throughout ramp-up
300-600s: All 10 threads running simultaneously, each looping independently
600s: Test ends - all threads stop wherever they are in their current loop</stringProp>
        <intProp name="ThreadGroup.num_threads">10</intProp>
        <intProp name="ThreadGroup.ramp_time">300</intProp>
        <longProp name="ThreadGroup.duration">600</longProp>
        <longProp name="ThreadGroup.delay">1</longProp>
        <boolProp name="ThreadGroup.same_user_on_next_iteration">true</boolProp>
        <boolProp name="ThreadGroup.scheduler">true</boolProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.on_sample_error">continue</stringProp>
        <elementProp name="ThreadGroup.main_controller" elementType="LoopController" guiclass="LoopControlPanel" testclass="LoopController" testname="Loop Controller">
          <intProp name="LoopController.loops">-1</intProp>
          <boolProp name="LoopController.continue_forever">false</boolProp>
        </elementProp>
      </ThreadGroup>
      <hashTree>
        <JSR223Sampler guiclass="TestBeanGUI" testclass="JSR223Sampler" testname="Generate common thread variables" enabled="true">
          <stringProp name="scriptLanguage">groovy</stringProp>
          <stringProp name="script">def rng = new java.util.Random()
def generateAblDate = {
    int currentYear = java.util.Calendar.getInstance().get(java.util.Calendar.YEAR)
    int year = currentYear + rng.nextInt(3)
    int month = 1 + rng.nextInt(12)
    int[] maxDays = [31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31]
    boolean leapYear = (year % 4 == 0) &amp;&amp; (year % 100 != 0 || year % 400 == 0)
    if (month == 2 &amp;&amp; leapYear) { maxDays[1] = 29 }
    int day = 1 + rng.nextInt(maxDays[month - 1])
    return String.format(&quot;%04d-%02d-%02d&quot;, year, month, day)
}
vars.put(&quot;shared_custNum&quot;, String.valueOf(10000 + rng.nextInt(90000)))
vars.put(&quot;shared_empNum&quot;, String.valueOf(10000 + rng.nextInt(90000)))
def companyData = props.get(&quot;companyData&quot;)
if (companyData != null &amp;&amp; companyData.size() &gt; 0) {
    def company = companyData[rng.nextInt(companyData.size())]
    vars.put(&quot;company_name&quot;, company.company_name)
    vars.put(&quot;company_franchise_sector&quot;, java.net.URLEncoder.encode(company.franchise + &quot; - &quot; + company.sector, &quot;UTF-8&quot;))
} else {
    vars.put(&quot;company_name&quot;, &quot;Test Corp&quot;)
    vars.put(&quot;company_franchise_sector&quot;, &quot;N%2FA&quot;)
}
vars.put(&quot;timesheet_dayRecorded&quot;, generateAblDate())
vars.put(&quot;vacation_startDate&quot;, generateAblDate())</stringProp>
          <stringProp name="parameters"></stringProp>
          <stringProp name="filename"></stringProp>
          <stringProp name="cacheKey">false</stringProp>
        </JSR223Sampler>
